+*Tranche 2, shelf-ready class extension.* The VEGFR multikinase extension, comprising regorafenib
+and lenvatinib together with the enumeration-surfaced nintedanib, sorafenib, axitinib, vandetanib
+and tivozanib, builds on the established active class in EMC and needs no new biomarker.
+Cabozantinib is not part of that extension and is not a hypothesis here: it has already been given
+to EMC patients. The phase II soft-tissue-sarcoma trial cited here as [19] enrolled three patients
+with EMC among 54 evaluable, reports one confirmed partial response in an EMC patient after ten
+cycles, and describes that as the longest response on the trial; the trial did not meet either of
+its primary endpoints, and its safety data are reported only for the whole mixed cohort. No efficacy
+conclusion for EMC is drawn here from a three-patient subgroup of a trial not powered for it. These are candidates for histology-inclusive basket trials of anti-angiogenic agents in
 sarcoma, or for prospective registry-embedded cohorts, with the caveat that they probably share the
 eventual resistance seen with pazopanib. Regional approval status varies by agent and would need
 checking before any such design.
